{"memo": "\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nALDERMOOR INDUSTRIES \u2014 CFO AUDIT MEMORANDUM\nDate: October 24, 2023\nRE: Procurement Request Audit Summary \u2014 Takumi Controls Europe B.V.\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\nThis memorandum synthesises the specialist audit reports for the procurement request from Takumi Controls Europe B.V. (\u20ac480,000 base value for Plant 1 industrial automation components). While Financial Control has validated the capital expenditure and Risk & Compliance has flagged high credit risk, the decisive factor governing this transaction is Treasury\u2019s identification of an active FX hedging variance breach. Per Aldermoor\u2019s delegation-of-authority matrix, the presence of a Treasury hold overrides standard approval pathways.\n\nKEY FINDINGS:\n\u2022 Risk & Compliance: REJECTED \u2014 Sanctions cleared, but vendor credit score of 45/100 triggers High Risk status for critical-path components, requiring senior escalation and financial security.\n\u2022 Tax & Treasury: HOLD FOR TREASURY AUDIT \u2014 Landed cost calculated at \u20ac586,080.00 (including \u20ac14,880 customs duty and \u20ac91,200 import VAT); FX variance of 6.04% breaches the \u00b15% hedging threshold.\n\u2022 IFRS Financial Control: APPROVED (Pending Dept Head sign-off) \u2014 Classified as CapEx under IAS 16.7 (GL 0200\u20130299, 7-year straight-line depreciation at \u20ac68,571.43 p.a.); threshold requirements met.\n\nFINAL DECISION: CONDITIONAL HOLD\nReason: Under Aldermoor governance rules, the presence of an FX alert and a Treasury hold requires a CONDITIONAL HOLD status. Payment release is blocked until the FX hedging variance is resolved, trade compliance confirms preferential tariff eligibility, and Risk & Compliance mitigation terms are satisfied.\n\nNEXT ACTIONS:\n1. Group Treasury & Global Procurement \u2014 Renegotiate or re-hedge the JPY/EUR currency exposure to bring the variance within the \u00b15% policy limit, and audit for potential EU-Japan EPA tariff exemptions \u2014 Deadline: 5 Business Days\n2. Global Procurement & Vendor (Takumi Controls) \u2014 Secure audited financials, full prepayment, or an acceptable bank guarantee to remediate the 45/100 credit score risk for this critical-path supply \u2014 Deadline: Prior to Purchase Order re-issuance\n3. Plant 1 Department Head \u2014 Formalize sign-off for the \u20ac480,000 CapEx addition (GL 0200\u20130299) in alignment with IFRS requirements \u2014 Deadline: Concurrent with commercial clearance\n\nSigned,\nCFO Office \u2014 Aldermoor Industries, Hamburg\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T04:26:03.823486Z", "level": "info", "severity": "INFO", "event": "CFO Synthesis complete"}
